\">19</a>, <a data-ref=\"Joshua 8:21\" href=\"/Joshua.8.21\">21</a>; <a data-ref=\"Judges 16:9\" href=\"/Judges.16.9\">Ju 16:9</a>, <a data-ref=\"Judges 16:12\" href=\"/Judges.16.12\">12</a>; <a data-ref=\"Judges 20:33\" href=\"/Judges.20.33\">20:33</a>, <a data-ref=\"Judges 20:36\" href=\"/Judges.20.36\">36</a>, <a data-ref=\"Judges 20:37\" href=\"/Judges.20.37\">37</a><sup>(×2)</sup>, <a data-ref=\"Judges 20:38\" href=\"/Judges.20.38\">38</a> <a data-ref=\"Ezra 8:31\" href=\"/Ezra.8.31\">Ezr 8:31</a>; pl. of this sing. = ambuscades <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 51:12\" href=\"/Jeremiah.51.12\">Je 51:12</a>; sg. = <em>place of lying-in-wait, ambush</em> (loc. sense) <a data-ref=\"Joshua 8:7\" href=\"/Joshua.8.7\">Jos 8:7</a>."}],"form":"Qal"},{"senses":[{"definition":"Pt. pl. <span dir=\"rtl\">מְאָֽרְבִים</span> <em>liers-in-wait</em>. <strong>Qal</strong> Pt. <a data-ref=\"Judges 9:25\" href=\"/Judges.9.25\">Ju 9:25</a> (c. <span dir=\"rtl\">ל</span>), <a data-ref=\"II Chronicles 20:22\" href=\"/II_Chronicles.20.22\">2 Ch 20:22</a> (c. <span dir=\"rtl\">עַל</span>).?"}],"form":"Pi."},{"senses":[{"definition":"Impf. <span dir=\"rtl\">וַיָּרֶב בנחל</span> (for <span dir=\"rtl\">וַיַּאֲרֶב</span>) <a data-ref=\"I Samuel 15:5\" href=\"/I_Samuel.15.5\">1 S 15:5</a> (cf. Dr Kö<sup>i 390</sup>; Ges-Kau<sup>§68. 2</sup> queries) but text dub.; cf. Ol<sup>§ 257 b</sup>, & Klo, who proposes <span dir=\"rtl\">ויעבר בנחל</span>."}],"form":"Hiph."}]},"rid":"BDB00789","strong_numbers":["693"],"next_hw":"אֶ֫רֶב","prev_hw":"אֶרְאֵל","all_cited":true,"root":true,"quotes":[],"GK":["741"],"TWOT":["156"],"parent_lexicon_details":{"name":"BDB Dictionary","language":"heb.biblical","to_language":"eng","text_categories":[],"source":"BDB Dictionary","attribution":"F. Brown, S. Driver & C. Briggs","index_title":"BDB","version_title":"A Hebrew and English lexicon of the Old Testament, by Francis Brown. With the co-operation of S. R. Driver and Charles A. Briggs. Oxford, 1906","version_lang":"en","